window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Do you find yourself constantly planning, but never doing?</p> <p>We've all experienced it. You know that you should get off the couch and exercise or stop scrolling through Facebook and finally get started on work.</p> <p>But something keeps us from taking action.</p> <p>Many people aren't able to identify exactly what it is, but they are more than familiar with the effect that inaction has on their life. Maybe you have been nagged by feelings of frustration or the belief that you will never be able to accomplish your goals.</p> <p>What many people don't know is that you already have the ability to achieve everything you've ever wanted.</p> <p>You have the power to control your thoughts, and your thoughts create the reality you live each day.</p> <p>Forming better habits and taking real steps toward your goals isn't as impossible it may appear to be. All that’s missing right now is for you to hone the mental abilities you already have.</p> <p>Kevin M. Hudson knows from experience just how powerful the subconscious mind can be, and he has compiled proven methods to help you transform your life as well.</p> <p>In <i>What You Imagine, You Create</i>, you will discover:</p> <ul> <li>The daily practice that will make articulating and accomplishing your goals easier than ever before</li> <li>Nine habits for personal and professional success that are practiced everyday by some of the most successful people in the world</li> <li>The simple technique to train your subconscious that successful actors, athletes, and business people swear by</li> <li>Five ways to get you into action and enable you to achieve all of your goals</li> <li>Step-by-step methods to integrate new practices into your life without needing to massively overhaul the routine you have now</li> <li>And much more</li> </ul> <p>If you're ready to think strategically and finally get started on your goals (and reach the finish line), then scroll up and click the “Buy Now” button right now.</p>"; 
